- Repository files were not modified by this draft.

Patch scope
- One existing file only: tests/integration/workflow-primitives/collection_end_result.rs
- Extends the genuine public scheduler-produced EXPRESSION_ERROR and pre-evaluation INSTANCE_LIMIT flows.
- Reconstructs each original Finish from retained finish sequence minus one, ordered checkpoint digests, scope/result/outbox identity, trace, retained event timestamp, and the current scheduler fence.
- Uses a fresh DefinitionCache and PgCollectionStore over flow.api.api_pool.
- The evaluated failure replay supplies EndOutputAnswer::ExpressionError; a supplied successful answer is rejected as DuplicateMismatch.
- The pre-evaluation refusal replay supplies no End answer; an unexpected ExpressionError answer is rejected as DuplicateMismatch.
- Both matching replays require applied=false and the retained current Run head.
- Before/after equality covers the Run, successful scope/owner, collection members and checkpoints, full Run journal, full tenant payload rows, run/tenant retained/tenant iteration usage, telemetry head, finish receipt fields, Run audits, and stable outbox fields.
- The replay command carries no aggregate body. PgCollectionStore accepts no expression evaluator or provider, so the cold call has no evaluation/provider path.

